  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine humanitarian winterization response for the most vulnerable and conflict-affected populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtDRC&apos;s proposed intervention is designed to address&#xA0;the significant increase in winterization needs due to increasing vulnerabilities (as the war is in its third year), basic needs gaps, and high sector-specific needs due to the targeted attacks on residential and critical energy infrastructure. The proposed intervention will meet acute winterization needs during the winter through the provision of fuel&#xA0;and utility assistance and the rehabilitation of collective sites hosting vulnerable displaced populations. DRC and implementing partners Angels of Salvation, City of Power, Lampa, and Pomogaem will ensure that the most vulnerable conflict-affected populations in Donetsk, Kharkiv, Zaporizhzhia, Dnipro, Mykolaiv, Kherson, Sumy, and Chernihiv have their winter needs met and avoid further reliance on negative coping mechanisms and increased exposure to protection violations to meet basic needs during the winter. The proposed intervention is fully aligned with the allocation strategy and cluster standards and recommendations, as evidenced by priority activities, modalities of assistance, and intervention areas. As a result of the proposed intervention, a minimum of 6,139&#xA0;households will receive support to meet winter fuel and energy needs, and up to 524&#xA0;individuals will be protected from winter exposure and experience improved living conditions through collective centre rehabilitation. DRC and partners commit to robust and ongoing national and subnational coordination to ensure that the impact of the proposed intervention will be maximized, duplication will be avoided, and those most in need will be prioritized for support. DRC will leverage strong protection technical capacity to ensure that protection is mainstreamed, and GBV and PSEA principles are applied across the scope of the intervention. The intervention builds upon the learning and experience from&#xA0;DRC&apos;s successful winterization response from 2023/2024, now including four of DRC&apos;s key humanitarian partners to provide support in amplifying the impact of the response while building their experience at winterization interventions with DRC&apos;s support.&#xA0;lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
